IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `insolv53-nouns`
IMPORT `insolv53-cross-references`

-- Row il-53. The recorded facts: the controls say what their instructions bring in, the printed figures agree between the official page and the consolidation excerpt where both exist, and what was read from where is what NOTES.md says.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their four failing assertions are in insolv53-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in insolv53-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the section of two paragraphs`

-- Away from the figure exactly one paragraph applies. These are the cases on which the two paragraphs agree with a reading in which they divide the debts between them.
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs of the section that apply to a total debt of` (`section: Execution Law s 7א2`) (0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs of the section that apply to a total debt of` (`section: Execution Law s 7א2`) (149999) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs of the section that apply to a total debt of` (`section: Execution Law s 7א2`) (150001) EQUALS 1
-- The first paragraph stops at the figure and the second starts at it; so each applies at the figure. This records that the defect is present; it does not say that the text is right.
#ASSERT `the paragraph applies to a total debt of` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(1)`) (150000)
#ASSERT `the paragraph applies to a total debt of` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(2)`) (150000)
#ASSERT `the number of paragraphs of the section that apply to a total debt of` (`section: Execution Law s 7א2`) (150000) EQUALS 2

§ `Tests of the printed figures`

-- The official page and the consolidation excerpt print the same figure in each paragraph of section 7א2 and in section 76(ג).
#ASSERT (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(1)`)'s `the figure in shekels` EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(2)`)'s `the figure in shekels` EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the figure the official instrument prints in the paragraph` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(1)`)
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the figure the official instrument prints in the paragraph` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(2)`)
#ASSERT (`figure: Execution Law s 76(ג), the fixed limit on the priority of a wage claim`)'s `the provision's figure in shekels` EQUALS 26000
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the figure the official instrument prints in the provision` (`figure: Execution Law s 76(ג), the fixed limit on the priority of a wage claim`)
-- The two figures of section 234(א)(1)(א) as enacted, from p. 366; the consolidation of the Insolvency Law was not deposited, so there is no second reading of them.
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for wages, as enacted`)'s `the provision's figure in shekels` EQUALS 25630
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for severance together with wages, as enacted`)'s `the provision's figure in shekels` EQUALS 39945
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for wages, as enacted`)'s `the consolidation prints the provision's figure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 234(ב), p. 366, says the enacted figures are updated each 1 January; the words that fix the Execution Law figure say nothing of updating.
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for wages, as enacted`)'s `the words that fix the figure also say it is updated each year`
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for severance together with wages, as enacted`)'s `the words that fix the figure also say it is updated each year`
#ASSERT (NOT (`figure: Execution Law s 76(ג), the fixed limit on the priority of a wage claim`)'s `the words that fix the figure also say it is updated each year`)

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- The two controls: the words each instruction brings in are the words in the consolidated target.
#ASSERT `the target as consolidated holds the words the instruction brings in` (`control: instruction (10) of s 361 to Execution Law s 77א`)
#ASSERT `the target as consolidated holds the words the instruction brings in` (`control: instruction (8) of s 361 to Execution Law s 69י1`)
-- The instruction of each control was read from the page image; its target's present words are CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, so neither control has both sides read from the official instruments.
#ASSERT (`control: instruction (10) of s 361 to Execution Law s 77א`)'s `the instruction was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`control: instruction (8) of s 361 to Execution Law s 69י1`)'s `the instruction was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (NOT `the instruction and the target were both read from the official instruments` (`control: instruction (10) of s 361 to Execution Law s 77א`))
#ASSERT (NOT `the instruction and the target were both read from the official instruments` (`control: instruction (8) of s 361 to Execution Law s 69י1`))

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Limb (a) of each figure was read from a page image; limb (b), that the present words are the words the instrument wrote, is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY for the Execution Law and `not read` for the Insolvency Law.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs of the paragraph were read from the official instruments` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(1)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs of the paragraph were read from the official instruments` (`paragraph: Execution Law s 7א2(2)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs of the provision were read from the official instruments` (`figure: Execution Law s 76(ג), the fixed limit on the priority of a wage claim`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs of the provision were read from the official instruments` (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for wages, as enacted`))
#ASSERT (`figure: Insolvency Law s 234(א)(1)(א), the figure for wages, as enacted`)'s `limb (b): that the present words of the provision are those words was read from` EQUALS `not read`
